## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design automated IR in Azure at scale, integrating Key Vault, Sentinel, Runbooks, and network isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Key Vault rotation and secret versioning
- Azure Sentinel detection rules and alerting
- Automation Runbooks or Logic Apps
- Private Endpoints and NSGs
- Azure AD session revocation and PIM

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-IR runbook snippet (Azure SDK)
async function rotateSecret(vaultName, secretName){
  const newValue = generateSecret();
  await secretClient.setSecret(vaultName, secretName, newValue);
  await aadClient.revokeUserSessions('compromised-id');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback path under partial failure?
- How do you ensure no downtime during rotation?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess practical crypto hygiene, CMEK provisioning, tenant isolation, and operations around rotating keys without service downtime.

## Key Concepts

- CMEK per tenant with Azure Key Vault
- Encryption at rest for Cosmos DB with CMEK
- Per-tenant Managed Identities and RBAC
- Key rotation automation and rollback
- Policy and monitoring integration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: create a CMEK and tie to Cosmos DB per tenant
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");
const { KeyClient } = require("@azure/keyvault-keys");
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const keyClient = new KeyClient(`https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net`, credential);
await keyClient.createKey("cosmos-cmek-tenantA", "RSA" );
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test key rotation without impacting customers?
- How do you handle key compromise or vault access revocation?
